  "content": {
    "id": "p43-q35-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "35",
    "prompt": "Given $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ are roots of $$x^2-6x+1=0,$$ find the quadratic equation with the given pairs of roots.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p43-q35-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$2\\alpha+1,\\ 2\\beta+1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x^2-14x+17=0$",
          "worked": "The original roots have $\\alpha+\\beta=6$ and $\\alpha\\beta=1$. Let the new roots be $A=2\\alpha+1$ and $B=2\\beta+1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}A+B&=2(\\alpha+\\beta)+2\\\\A+B&=2(6)+2\\\\A+B&=14\\\\AB&=4\\alpha\\beta+2(\\alpha+\\beta)+1\\\\AB&=4(1)+2(6)+1\\\\AB&=17\\end{align*}$$\nUsing $x^2-(A+B)x+AB=0$, the required equation is $$x^2-14x+17=0.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 92
      },
      {
        "id": "p43-q35-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac1\\alpha,\\ \\dfrac1\\beta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x^2-6x+1=0$",
          "worked": "Let $A=\\dfrac1\\alpha$ and $B=\\dfrac1\\beta$.\n$$\\begin{align*}A+B&=\\frac{\\alpha+\\beta}{\\alpha\\beta}\\\\A+B&=\\frac61\\\\A+B&=6\\\\AB&=\\frac1{\\alpha\\beta}\\\\AB&=1\\end{align*}$$\nUsing $x^2-(A+B)x+AB=0$, the required equation is $$x^2-6x+1=0.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 72
      },
      {
        "id": "p43-q35-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\alpha^4,\\ \\beta^4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p43-q35-c-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "x^2-1154x+1=0",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p43-q35-c-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Apply the sum-of-squares identity twice to find the new sum of roots.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\alpha^2+\\beta^2&=(\\alpha+\\beta)^2-2\\alpha\\beta\\\\\\alpha^2+\\beta^2&=6^2-2(1)\\\\\\alpha^2+\\beta^2&=34\\end{align*}$$\nLet $A=\\alpha^4$ and $B=\\beta^4$.\n$$\\begin{align*}A+B&=(\\alpha^2+\\beta^2)^2-2\\alpha^2\\beta^2\\\\A+B&=34^2-2(1)^2\\\\A+B&=1154\\\\AB&=(\\alpha\\beta)^4\\\\AB&=1\\end{align*}$$\nThe required equation is $$x^2-1154x+1=0.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 92
      },
      {
        "id": "p43-q35-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\alpha-\\beta,\\ \\beta-\\alpha$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x^2-32=0$",
          "worked": "Let $A=\\alpha-\\beta$ and $B=\\beta-\\alpha$.\n$$\\begin{align*}A+B&=0\\\\AB&=-(\\alpha-\\beta)^2\\\\AB&=-\\bigl((\\alpha+\\beta)^2-4\\alpha\\beta\\bigr)\\\\AB&=-\\bigl(6^2-4(1)\\bigr)\\\\AB&=-32\\end{align*}$$\nUsing $x^2-(A+B)x+AB=0$, the required equation is $$x^2-32=0.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 68
      }
    ]
